Subject: metal 0021: blit encoder (texture/buffer copies, mipmaps, fill)

MTLBlitCommandEncoder for the Metal driver, recorded like the compute encoder and run in
order at -commit. Library (tools/mesa/air/air_metal.[ch]): rwa_texture_copy and
rwa_buffer_copy (pipe->resource_copy_region), rwa_texture_gen_mipmap (util_gen_mipmap,
linear), rwa_buffer_fill (pipe->clear_buffer, else map+memset after a finish); each waits
like rwa_render_clear (deferred under rwa_set_deferred_wait). Driver
(userland/src/redwoodmetal.m): RedwoodMetalBlitEncoder; texture<->buffer copies by the
CPU at replay time (rwa_finish, then rwa_texture_read/rwa_texture_write per image with
bytesPerRow); sync/fence/optimize selectors are no-ops. -blitCommandEncoder answers nil
when the library lacks any of the four calls (older library: unchanged behaviour).

diff --git a/tools/mesa/air/air_metal.h b/tools/mesa/air/air_metal.h
index ffe4191..f773fbb 100644
--- a/tools/mesa/air/air_metal.h
+++ b/tools/mesa/air/air_metal.h
@@ -1469,6 +1469,38 @@ int rwa_render_clear(struct rwa_device *device, struct rwa_texture *const *color
 		     const float *clear_depth, const unsigned *clear_stencil,
 		     char *why, size_t why_size);
 
+/*
+ * 0021: what MTLBlitCommandEncoder asks of the GPU. Each is queued on the device's context
+ * and waited for like rwa_render_clear: at once, or with rwa_set_deferred_wait on by the
+ * caller's next rwa_finish or rwa_flush. 0, or -1 and a sentence. New in 0021: absent in
+ * older libraries.
+ *
+ * rwa_texture_copy: `size` texels (NULL: the whole source level) from `src_origin` of
+ * level/slice of `src` to `dst_origin` of level/slice of `dst`. A NULL origin is (0,0,0).
+ * The texels move as bytes, so both formats must have the same texel size and kind
+ * (colour, or depth/stencil) and the same sample count.
+ */
+int rwa_texture_copy(struct rwa_device *device, struct rwa_texture *src, unsigned src_level,
+		     unsigned src_layer, const unsigned src_origin[3], const unsigned size[3],
+		     struct rwa_texture *dst, unsigned dst_level, unsigned dst_layer,
+		     const unsigned dst_origin[3], char *why, size_t why_size);
+
+/* 0021: `size` bytes from `src_offset` of `src` to `dst_offset` of `dst`, on the GPU. Two
+ * ranges of one buffer must not overlap. */
+int rwa_buffer_copy(struct rwa_device *device, struct rwa_buffer *src, size_t src_offset,
+		    struct rwa_buffer *dst, size_t dst_offset, size_t size,
+		    char *why, size_t why_size);
+
+/* 0021: every level of `texture` after the first, each a linear reduction of the one
+ * before, over every slice. A texture of one level is 0 and touches nothing. */
+int rwa_texture_gen_mipmap(struct rwa_device *device, struct rwa_texture *texture,
+			   char *why, size_t why_size);
+
+/* 0021: `size` bytes at `offset` of `buffer` set to `value`: on the GPU when the driver has
+ * a fill, otherwise through the buffer's mapping after the queued work has finished. */
+int rwa_buffer_fill(struct rwa_device *device, struct rwa_buffer *buffer, size_t offset,
+		    size_t size, unsigned char value, char *why, size_t why_size);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
